{"agent":"fleet-testpollution","data":{"budget":"","claim":"A suite run under a git hook inherits GIT_DIR/GIT_INDEX_FILE, which override git -C, so fixtures' git init/config/commit act on the repo running the gate","dedupe":{"answer":"new","candidates":[],"score":null},"falsifier":"a clone with GIT_DIR exported shows no Test identity / init commit after running tests/test_cli.py","item":"fix-B1d82c6b76f","mechanism":"git ignores -C when GIT_DIR is set; core.bare comes from git init --bare, identity from git config, init commits from the repo fixture","probe":"GIT_DIR=<clone>/.git pytest tests/test_cli.py -k 'collide or init' in a clone; then git log and git config --local --list","probe_output":"clone HEAD became 'Test init' (author Test <[REDACTED:email]>, README.md 6473 lines deleted), config gained user.name=Test, user.email=[REDACTED:email]; without GIT_DIR a 8% partial run (shim logging every mutating git call with cwd in the copy) logged nothing but git init <tmp path>","question":"Why does the suite write to the real repo?","sources":[],"verdict":"CONFIRMED"},"id":"e8962b71e5eaff2139c4f5700","kind":"research.recorded","lamport":71143,"schema":1,"subject":"Rd1dae6c2ea","ts":"2026-10-16T21:25:34.947553Z"}
